WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:06.580
So should I just do it now?

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:07.580
Yup.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:11.250
President Obama: That's how we forged a Trans-Pacific
Partnership, to open markets and protect workers

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:15.549
and the environment, and advance American
leadership in Asia.

00:00:15.549 --> 00:00:23.460
It cuts 18,000 taxes on products made in America,
which will then support more good jobs here

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.180
in America.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:28.550
With TPP, China does not set the rules in
that region, we do.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:32.232
Derek: President Obama mentioned the Trans-Pacific
Partnership in his speech tonight, but he

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:33.860
should have said a lot more.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:38.280
One reason that he didn't say more may be
that he's in favor, but Democratic presidential

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.329
candidate Hillary Clinton is opposed.

00:00:40.329 --> 00:00:44.590
On the Republican side, Ted Cruz is opposed,
Jeb Bush is in favor.

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:47.989
The reason for all this disagreement is that
Trans-Pacific Partnership is a really big

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:48.989
deal.

00:00:48.989 --> 00:00:50.079
It's 6,000 pages long.

00:00:50.079 --> 00:00:53.710
It's going to affect America in a lot of ways,
now and in the future.

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:58.030
One positive thing the President mentioned,
it's going to cut taxes on 18,000 goods and

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:02.000
services that are coming into the United States,
making them cheaper for ordinary Americans.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.489
But the President also said it allows us to
make the rules instead of China, and that's

00:01:05.489 --> 00:01:07.460
not really true.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:11.350
The rules on intellectual property, on state
owned enterprises, on services exports in

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:14.700
which American firms are the best in the world,
they're all too weak.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.240
We need to change them.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.909
President Obama talked about looking toward
the future, and in the future the TPP is only

00:01:19.909 --> 00:01:23.530
going to get more important to the U.S., but
if it were to help the U.S., we need to make

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:24.530
it better.

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:27.290
And if we can't make it better under President
Obama, then we're going to need to make it

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:30.990
better under the next President.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.270
So what are your thoughts on President Obama's
legacy?

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:37.020
Let us know in the comments, and check out
these other videos by AEI scholars.

